Subtract when a smaller symbol precedes a larger one, for example IX is 10 - 1.

code:
values = {'I': 1, 'V': 5, 'X': 10}
s = 'IX'
total = 0
for i, ch in enumerate(s):
    if i + 1 < len(s) and values[ch] < values[s[i + 1]]:
        total -= values[ch]
    else:
        total += values[ch]
print(total)  # 9

real example:
Parsing Roman numerals in puzzles and games.

